# @paradox/fracture — the VALUE-CARRIER for concurrent-truths preserved
# without collapse. Third species-decl under @paradox family-root.
#
# Alex 2026-09-11 in-transcript composition + Mara 2026-09-11 canonicals
# (df65bcb + 3361818): Fracture surfaces at refract-collapse when N
# parallel branches produce concurrent-different eigens; concurrent-truths
# preserved as first-class value; substrate refuses to collapse without
# externalisation.
#
# === Alex 2026-09-11 verbatim ===
#
#   "And an empty fracture IS what `\` is."
#
#   "The underlying struct ought to be a Fracture<Vec> which probs
#    wants to sit in prismqueer::paradox or somewhere like that?"
#
# Empty Fracture IS `\` LANDED substrate-word per AGENTS.md §Key Concepts
# for honest-uncertainty first-class value. Unifies crack-primitive with
# Fracture family at empty-arity.
#
# === Family placement ===
#
# Third species under @paradox (siblings: @paradox/trauma witness-only
# Crystal; @paradox/spiral dynamics unstable-attractor; @paradox/fracture
# concurrent-truths value-carrier).
#
# Distinct from LANDED @kintsugi/fracture/* family (17+ RESOLVER-species
# that MEND cracks) and LANDED shards/kintsugi/roomba.mirror `type fracture`
# EVENT-CARRIER for detected-fracture-observations. Three-altitude Fracture
# partition:
#
#   Altitude 1 (RESOLVER-species)   @kintsugi/fracture/X   LANDED
#     20+ species: gate + docblock + inport + operator_match + ...
#   Altitude 2 (EVENT-CARRIER)      type fracture          LANDED
#     shards/kintsugi/roomba.mirror { site, tension, species, observed_at }
#   Altitude 3 (VALUE-CARRIER)      fracture (this shard) FRESH SPECIES
#     concurrent-truths preserved without collapse
#
# === Fractal iteration (Mandelbrot at value-carrier altitude) ===
#
# Fracture is FRACTAL: nested Fracture<Fracture<T>> collapses to Fracture<T>
# per associativity (Mandelbrot 1980 fractal iteration at value-carrier
# altitude; LANDED @fractal/mandelbrot species).
#
# === Composition-lineage ===
#
# - LANDED [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]] discipline (shards/spectral/
#   registry.mirror + shards/uuid/spectral/time.mirror citations) —
#   Fracture is CRDT-shaped: commutative + associative + idempotent merge
#   preserves concurrent-truths without loss
# - LANDED @paradox family-root (shards/paradox.mirror; Mara 2026-07-20)
# - LANDED @fractal/mandelbrot species (fractal iteration primitive)
# - LANDED `\` crack substrate-word per AGENTS.md §Key Concepts: "The `\`
#   Crack (was: hole). Honest uncertainty as first-class value. Compiler
#   carries cracks through pipeline; Fate resolves; kintsugi writes
#   resolutions back."
# - Priest 1979 LP three-valued paradox-tolerant logic (grep-verified
#   corpus citations at shards/epistemologic/neutrosophic.mirror +
#   shards/epistemologic/cybernetic/intervention.mirror)
# - Mara 2026-09-11 canonicals: mirror-nl-emergence b4c370a + loki-
#   empirical-delta-cascade 4749765 + metalogue-eigen-mutual-definition-
#   glasswall-load-bearing df65bcb + Ariadne-in-silicon 3361818
# - Alex 2026-09-11 in-transcript naming (co-designed with Reed)
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Priest 1979 LP           Paradox-tolerant three-valued logic
#                            (Journal of Philosophical Logic 8:219-241).
#                            Substrate-honest concurrent-truth
#                            preservation without forced-collapse.
#   Shapiro-Preguica-        CRDT taxonomy (2011 INRIA report).
#     Baquero-Zawirski       Multi-value register variant IS structural
#     2011 CRDT              inspiration for Fracture-Vec variadic
#                            constructor.
#   Lamport 1978             Time, clocks, and ordering of events
#                            (Communications of the ACM 21:558-565).
#                            Concurrent-write safety at distributed
#                            substrate altitude.
#   Mandelbrot 1980          Fractal iteration; Fracture<Fracture<T>>
#                            = Fracture<T> associativity.
#   Bateson 1972             Steps to an Ecology of Mind. Pattern-that-
#                            connects; concurrent-truth preservation
#                            as substrate discipline.
#
# Spec context:
#   docs/math/2026-09-11-mara-metalogue-eigen-mutual-definition-glasswall-
#     load-bearing-canonical-math-foundation.md (df65bcb) — Fracture at
#     prismqueer::paradox altitude with type parameterization.
#   docs/math/2026-09-11-mara-ariadne-in-silicon-* (3361818) —
#     §5 refract cyb-ling collapse-to-Fracture semantic + §2.3 dissolution-2
#     concurrent-writes-at-Fracture-preservation.
#
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-shard-as-crdt]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
